; bfsodium BLOCKLOOP : the ChaCha20 block function as loops
;
; HAND WRITTEN skeleton; @@QR@@ @@ROWROT@@ and @@STAGGER@@ paste routines that
; are each already verified on their own  and each appears ONCE;
;
; INTERFACE entry=63 exit=0 footprint=0:271
;
; IO  in:  key{32}  counter{4} LE  nonce{12}        (48 bytes)
;     out: keystream block{64}                      (64 bytes)
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x00:0x3f  state{16}   u32 LE  the sixteen words  row major
;   @0x40:0x47  rowtmp{8}   u8      rowrot and stagger stage words here; their
;                                   footprint is @0x00:0x47  which is EIGHT
;                                   temps and not four  because stagger's row 2
;                                   exchanges the row's two halves in one go;
;                                   orig used to sit at @0x44 while stagger's
;                                   own header claimed four  and one word of
;                                   every block came out with the ASCII of
;                                   expand added to it; tools/bffoot now proves
;                                   every declared footprint against the
;                                   instruction stream  so the numbers here rest
;                                   on a check and not on a promise;
;   @0x48:0x87  orig{16}    u32 LE  a copy  added back at the end
;   @0x88:0xc2  QR frame            its operands are @0x88:0x97
;   @0xc3:0xc7  a gap               so a routine that grew would land in nothing
;                                   rather than in the counters
;   @0xc8:0xcd  counters            columns @0xc8  passes @0xc9  staggers @0xcb
;                                   rounds @0xcc  words @0xcd
;   @0xd0:0x10f copytmp{64} u8      temps for duplicating the state
; read the key  counter and nonce into words four through fifteen
; The sixteen arrows step over the constant  which is written below rather than
; above; A routine is pasted from its read onwards  so the read must come first
; and no instruction may precede it  or a caller would silently lose it;
  >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
                                                               ; continued
  >,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
                                                               ; continued
  >,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
